      "description": "Kawachi Wisteria Garden is a private hillside garden famous for its spectacular 80m and 110m long tunnels of cascading wisteria blossoms in shades of purple, pink, and white. The garden is open only during wisteria season (late April to mid-May) and autumn foliage season. Reservations are essential during peak bloom.",
